# Project: KeySync Lite – Real Estate Lead Intelligence MVP

## Tech & Architecture

- Backend: Node.js + Express serving a lead-intelligence API and static frontend.
- Frontend (legacy): Plain HTML/CSS/JS in `/public`.
- Frontend (new work): Use React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS. Prefer functional components and hooks.

## UI & UX Guidelines

- Overall vibe: Modern SaaS dashboard, dark theme, Dubai real-estate aesthetics (subtle luxury, not flashy).
- Layout:
  - Left panel: Customer View (chat-style message interface).
  - Right panel: Intelligence View (multi-column analysis: pipeline, persona/routing, scoring/insights).
- Components:
  - Use reusable components for: Chat layout, Message bubble, Tag/badge, Card, Tabs.
- Responsiveness:
  - Must work beautifully on desktop and reasonably on tablet/mobile (stack panels vertically on small screens).

## Code Style

- Use TypeScript for all new frontend files.
- Use Tailwind utility classes rather than inline styles or raw CSS when possible.
- Keep components small and composable. Move complex UI logic into custom hooks.

## AI Expectations for Cursor

- When adding UI features, update or create React components instead of editing legacy static HTML where possible.
- Preserve existing backend API contracts; if a change is needed, propose it clearly in comments.
- Always explain major refactors with a short comment at the top of the PR or file.
